{"id":750,"date":"2016-09-20T13:26:36","date_gmt":"2016-09-20T13:26:36","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/ibafflatusdesign.space\/?p=750"},"modified":"2017-02-05T02:04:19","modified_gmt":"2017-02-05T02:04:19","slug":"parliament-vienna-austria","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/travel-log\/parliament-vienna-austria\/","title":{"rendered":"Parliament, Vienna, Austria"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>The Austrian Parliament serves as the home of the National Council (<i>Nationalrat<\/i>) and the Federal Council (<i>Bundesrat<\/i>). One of the most important ceremonies to take place at the Parliament is the swearing in of the Austrian president. Ironically though, while Emperor Franz Joseph commissioned the building, he never actually stepped foot in it. Additionally, with representatives from eight nations, the multinational parliament had ineffective communication. The lack of translation in parliament provided such frustrations that representatives would often play instruments and bang on the tables to annoy each other. While the start of the Austrian Parliament was anything but smooth, it was most definitely an important step for the democratic nation.<\/p>\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-1034 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox-free fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-small fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-1034\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:false},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/02\/DSC_1283.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Theophil von Hasen built Parliament in the Greek style in order to symbolize democracy. He decorated the front with bronze statues of horse tamers to show that a successful National Assembly must keep its emotions in check. Finally, a fountain featuring the Greek Goddess Athena, a symbol of wisdom, is placed at the forefront.\" data-attachment-id=\"1036\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Theophil von Hasen built Parliament in the Greek style in order to symbolize democracy. He decorated the front with bronze statues of horse tamers to show that a successful National Assembly must keep its emotions in check. Finally, a fountain featuring the Greek Goddess Athena, a symbol of wisdom, is placed at the forefront.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2017\/02\/DSC_1283\/2097101294.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Theophil von Hasen built Parliament in the Greek style in order to symbolize democracy. He decorated the front with bronze statues of horse tamers to show that a successful National Assembly must keep its emotions in check. Finally, a fountain featuring the Greek Goddess Athena, a symbol of wisdom, is placed at the forefront.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/02\/IMAG4117.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Construction started in 1873. By 1883 the building was complete, but it took another twenty years to complete all of the details on the inside.\" data-attachme